---
<LandingLayout
  title="Microsoft Publisher Content Marketplace and FORA — FORA resources"
  description="How Microsoft's pilot marketplace licenses publishers' content to Copilot for cited answers, what it asks of your site, where it is ahead of FORA, and how a publisher can use both."
>
  <AudienceHero
    current="resources"
    badge={`Resources · ${a('/resources/content-marketplaces/', 'Content marketplaces')} · Microsoft PCM`}
    title="Microsoft's marketplace comes with Microsoft as the buyer. <em>On FORA, any agent can buy, at a price you set before the sale.</em>"
    sub="Microsoft's Publisher Content Marketplace (PCM) licenses your content to AI products, mainly for grounding, where the AI uses your article to answer one question, and shows it as a cited link. Copilot is its first buyer. On FORA, an open protocol, any AI agent can buy each page on terms and at a price you set."
    updated={resourceUpdated(HREF)}
  >
    <a href="#ahead" class="btn btn-primary">Where PCM is ahead</a>
    <a href="#together" class="btn btn-ghost">Use both</a>
  </AudienceHero>

  <Band tone="near" id="glance" label="At a glance" title="PCM and FORA, side by side" lead={`Microsoft has published one launch post, one product page and interviews about PCM. Where this page shows ${NP}, those documents don't say.`}>
    <GlanceCard vendor="Microsoft PCM" groups={GLANCE} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="The short answer" title="A buyer under contract, or an interface any agent can use">
    <CardGrid items={SHORT_ANSWER} />
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.exchange} />
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.edgeFunction} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="How you're paid" title={'Microsoft pays "on delivered value". The unit isn\'t published.'} lead={`For Copilot's use, Microsoft is the buyer. It says "publishers will be paid on delivered value" (${a(M.launch, 'launch post')}). The payable unit, who sets the price and when you're paid: ${NP}`} asideWidth="440px" asideAlign="start">
    <StepList slot="intro" items={PAID_STEPS} />
    <Figure
      slot="aside"
      src={`${IMG}/pcm-1.png`}
      title="Microsoft PCM, from an interest form to a payment."
      alt="Microsoft PCM in six steps: you register interest, sign a contract negotiated one by one in the pilot, hand over content, set the terms (Grounding and Display, not training), Copilot uses it while Yahoo is being onboarded, and you're paid. How publishers are selected, how content is handed over (feed, API or crawl), the terms' vocabulary, and the unit, price and report are not public. Beside step 5, separate from PCM, is Bing's crawl; how Bing's settings affect a PCM license is not public either."
    />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" compact label="PCM in four numbers">
    <KeyFacts items={KEY_FACTS} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="Who has signed, and who has been paid" title="Seven publishers named, four confirmed. No payment is public.">
    <PullQuote
      quote="People Inc. has signed a deal with Microsoft to partner as one of a select group of premier publishers to build Microsoft’s Publisher Content Marketplace (PCM)."
      who="IAC, People Inc's owner"
      source="third-quarter 2025 results"
      href={M.iac}
    />
    <p class="prose" set:html={`Microsoft names seven US co-design publishers, "among others": The Associated Press, Business Insider, Condé Nast, Hearst Magazines, People Inc, USA TODAY Co. and Vox Media ${cite(1)}. Four confirmed their deals in late 2025: Gannett, in its ${a(M.gannett, 'third-quarter results')}; People Inc, through its owner ${a(M.iac, 'IAC')}; the AP, to ${a(M.ap, 'Digiday')}; and Business Insider, in a ${a(M.bi, 'staff memo')}.`} />
    <p class="prose">Microsoft publishes no count of publishers. Neither Microsoft nor a publisher has said a payment was made.</p>
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="What it takes on your site" title="PCM documents nothing on your site. FORA is a file and an edge function." lead="PCM's column is what Microsoft documents. Microsoft Learn's search returns no page on PCM, and Microsoft's help and webmaster sites carry no publisher integration guide for it.">
    <Split>
      <div>
        <h3 class="sub-h col-h">PCM</h3>
        <PointList tone="neutral" items={SITE_PCM} />
      </div>
      <div slot="aside">
        <h3 class="sub-h col-h">FORA</h3>
        <PointList items={SITE_FORA} />
      </div>
    </Split>
    <div class="callout-gap">
      <Callout kind="engineers" collapse="Show the five steps">
        <StepList fora items={ENGINEER_STEPS} />
      </Callout>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" id="search-traffic" label="Search traffic" title="Bing's crawl is separate from PCM, and it feeds Copilot too" lead={`Bing's crawl feeds "web-grounded responses in Bing, Copilot, and Microsoft 365" (${a(M.bing, 'Bing')}). From February 1, 2027, Bing reads new preferences as it crawls: one for AI training and one for grounding, both apart from search. "These settings govern use of content, not crawl access." How any of them affects a PCM license: ${NP} FORA's ${a('/resources/ai-crawlers/#generator', 'rules generator')} writes Bing's training refusal on every setting, and its grounding refusal only if you leave AI search.`} asideWidth="400px" asideAlign="start">
    <Figure
      slot="aside"
      src={`${IMG}/pcm-3.png`}
      title="What each of Bing's settings does."
      alt="Three Bing settings: refuse training in robots.txt per site or path, or per page; refuse grounding per page only, with a meta tag or response header, which keeps you in Bing search and significantly reduces your visibility in AI answers; or block Bingbot and drop out of Bing search. Bing reads the new preferences from February 1, 2027, and after March 1, 2027, NoArchive and NoCache stop counting for training and grounding."
    />
    <Callout kind="caution" points={CAUTIONS}>
      <PullQuote
        small
        quote="[Refusing grounding] will significantly reduce your content’s visibility in AI-generated experiences, without affecting eligibility for Bing search results."
        who="Bing"
        source="Your content, your choice: clearer preferences for training and grounding"
        href={M.bing}
      />
    </Callout>
    <Callout kind="search" text={SEARCH_FORA.text} links={SEARCH_FORA.links}>
      <p>PCM documents nothing that touches search crawlers. Bing's crawl, above, is a separate route into Copilot.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Band>

  <Band id="ahead" label="Where PCM is ahead" title="What PCM does that FORA doesn't">
    <PointList tone="neutral" items={AHEAD} />
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.dealTerm} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" label="The differences, question by question" title="Eight questions a publisher asks of any licensing deal" lead="PCM does the first four inside one company's contract; FORA does them with a public file and signed messages. The last four compare like for like.">
    <Callout kind="define" {...DEFINITIONS.broker} />
    <CompareTable vendor="Microsoft PCM" rows={COMPARE} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="near" id="together" label="Running both" title="Both on one site today">
    <h3 class="sub-h">Works today</h3>
    <PointList items={WORKS} />
    <figure class="term-card">
      <CodeCard head="For AI answers, not training. Credit the article." rows={TERM_LINES} label="Grounding and Display as one FORA term." />
      <figcaption>Grounding and Display as one FORA term.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p class="prose" set:html={`The difference is the price. PCM pays "on delivered value", by a unit Microsoft hasn't published ${cite(1)}. On FORA, the price is signed on the offer before the sale. An agent that isn't a PCM buyer finds this term through the file that names your Exchanges.`} />
    <h3 class="sub-h">Doesn't fit</h3>
    <p class="prose" set:html={`<b>Paying FORA sales through PCM.</b> PCM is a marketplace with Microsoft as the payer, and no payment service for others. On FORA, the Exchange operator bills the buyer and pays you (${a(D.howItWorks, 'What is FORA?')}).`} />
    <p class="prose" set:html={`<b>Declaring PCM in a file.</b> Microsoft publishes no file or tag that says a site is in PCM. Asked whether RSL could work with PCM, Microsoft's spokesperson didn't have "anything specific to share today" (${a(M.verge, 'The Verge')}, February 3, 2026). Say it on your licensing page, in words.`} />
  </Band>

  <Band label="What to do" title="If you're in PCM, or weighing it">
    <PointList numbered items={TODO} />
    <Callout kind="legal" points={LEGAL} />
  </Band>

  <Band tone="light" id="about">
    <Callout kind="about" points={ABOUT_FORA} columns />
    <section class="sources" id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-label">
      <h2 class="end-label" id="sources-label">Sources</h2>
      <p class="note">Sources are checked on the date of publication.</p>
      <SourceList groups={SOURCES} compact numbered />
    </section>
    <SeriesNav current={HREF} />
  </Band>

  <ClosingCta
    title="Put a price any agent can read <em>on your content</em>"
    text="FORA is an open protocol and free, open-source software. Sell through any FORA marketplace, several of them, or your own: you set terms and a price per resource, and each Exchange signs your offers."
  >
    <a href="/protocol/licensing-terms/" class="btn btn-primary">Licensing terms</a>
    <a href="/getting-started/existing-marketplace/" class="btn btn-ghost">Run your own marketplace</a>
    <a href="/resources/content-marketplaces/" class="btn btn-ghost">All content marketplaces</a>
    <a href="/components/edge-function/deployment/" class="btn btn-ghost">What FORA takes on your CDN</a>
  </ClosingCta>
</LandingLayout>

